# roadmaps/realtime.md R0 across a kill and a start (roadmap l4.md L12,
# L13): the clock killed, everything made for it revoked a capability at a
# time with a window after each, then built again; the kernel still never
# keeps interrupts off for half a tick. Without the windows a kill is one
# stretch over every slot of every space, for each capability it deletes.
program: shell
define: TEST_STRETCH
define: TEST_DEMO
keys: {wait 100}kill clock\n{wait 50}start clock\n{wait 50}
timeout: 60
emulators: bochs mame
match: contains
---
rx286: interrupts never off for 10 ms
